# Auto-generated by scripts/generate-sitemap.js (prebuild) -- source of truth
# is scripts/public-routes.js + src/data/blogs.ts, both tracked.
# public/sitemap.xml is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It is generated by scripts/generate-sitemap.js in the prebuild hook, and a
# generated artefact in git is normally a smell. But the host runs whatever build
# command its dashboard is configured with, and if that is `vite build` rather
# than `npm run build` the npm lifecycle hooks never fire -- which is exactly
# what happened: production served the SPA shell for /sitemap.xml, and Search
# Console reported "Couldn't fetch" with 0 pages discovered.
#
# Committing it means the sitemap ships even when no hook runs. The generator
# still keeps it current; this only removes the single point of failure.

# Environment variables — NEVER commit secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
